  <ym-title|Sharp centered and fixed-arity
  bounds><label|sharp-centered-and-fixed-arity-bounds>

  Fragment <verbatim|chapters/13-sharp-bounds.tex>, for root integration. The
  phase paragraph naturally belongs after Chapter15's compression algebra if
  forward references are to be avoided. No master edits.

  Exports ch13:sharp-schedule, sharp-root, sharp-centered, first-below,
  sharp-separated, sharp-phase. Exact primary root source: Scott
  E-several-mark78\U120, E-section354\U377. Uses current11
  replicated-bound/root-bound with weighted singleton x=3,y=1 and complete
  higher-mode arrays. UV confirms decreasing all weights preserves termwise
  ordinary/forced incidence; this argument does NOT use its large-weight
  detector Gaussian comparison.

  Weights omega_k=a_k^d beta_k^-w_d/E_k where E_k is inverse-column product
  including terminal column. Existing local section/threshold and source
  attachment estimates require finitely many inversebeta powers at
  fixeddegree; choosew_d once to absorb them. logE=o(tau) by ratio/column
  conditions, logbeta=o(tau), so\<minus\>logomega=d tau+o(tau). All
  eligibility events and incoming higher modes retained.

  Coarse Haar-ball normalization q_site=O_j(1+logbeta) suffices. It uses
  admissible global scalar-free exponent upper bound C_jV and
  small-link-event lower bound\<minus\>C_jV; leading action on
  linksrho=beta^-1/2 costs C_j beta rho\<twosuperior\>V. This is the explicit
  action-class bound behind ScottE normalization-cost, not refined3V+1
  versus3V\<minus\>3 Gaussian cancellation. If those global action-class
  costs were weakened to O(beta), this argument would not give sharpdegree;
  do not replace them by a full absolute bound on the positive leading
  action.

  Additional selected schedule floors must be retained:
  B_i+1\<twosuperior\>\<less\>=2B_i\<twosuperior\>, (L_i
  B_i\<twosuperior\>)^4q_site_i+1=o(tau_i+1), column log ratioso1,
  transitions lognewcolumn=o(tau). Fixedstage
  B<strike-through|log\<twosuperior\>tau,q>logtau makes them feasible by
  delayedentry after ratiosfixed. Firstsparse stopping k(m) gives Wq=o(tau_k)
  andtau_k/tau_m\<rightarrow\>1. Finite initiallevels absorbed into
  oneconstant fixed BEFOREm. Cutoffthreshold maydependm, uniformlyp.

  SlowratioslogL=o(tau) imply firstscale belowcr has
  tau/log1/r\<rightarrow\>1; apply twice for coarsecell then
  interiorcenteredcell. Fixedarity loss is
  r^\<minus\>sumdegrees\<minus\>epsilon, rather than priorr^\<minus\>4(d+1)n.
  Derivative labels require the existing quotientcalculus; no new derivative
  theorem inferred.

  Phaseuniformity: whole-word compressedoperator moments use arbitrarily many
  copies placed at cell-aligned far translations, so fixed one-word
  scales/bounds suffice. Faithful ground-state momentnorm andcharacters give
  samebound EVERYphase. Never estimate phasevalue by mixedvalue ofsameword
  directly.

  No new literature proof: elementary scalealgebra and existing abstract
  chessboard theorem already checked/cited in Chapters1/13; source-specific
  weight optimization is proved in fragment. Standalone3pages, no
  overfull/underfull boxes; root handlesglobalrender.
